      "search:sku": "019S-06370",
      "search:title": "Advanced Training: Influenza &amp; RSV WGS Using Oxford Nanopore Technology",
      "search:description": "The Public Health Laboratories of Hellenic Pasteur Institute (HPI) offer a comprehensive 5-day training course on Next-Generation Sequencing (NGS) for Influenza and Respiratory Syncytial Virus (RSV), using Oxford Nanopore Technology. This course is designed to provide participants with the knowledge and practical skills required to perform whole-genome sequencing and analysis of two major respiratory viruses—Influenza and RSV—supporting surveillance, research, and diagnostic development. Participants will have the opportunity to engage in real-life Influenza and RSV practises at the National Influenza Reference Laboratory of Southern Greece.\r\nParticipants will gain both theoretical knowledge and hands-on experience in key NGS workflows, including:\r\n1. Viral RNA extraction for NGS applications,\r\n2. Library preparation for multiplexed sequencing, \r\n3. Operation of Oxford Nanopore platforms, \r\n4. Data Processing Workflow: Basecalling, Alignment, and Assembly,\r\n5. NGS data quality control and validation, \r\n6. Basic bioinformatics pipelines for Influenza and RSV virus genomics,\r\n7. Bioinformatics tools for variant analysis and mutation detection. \r\nA special rate will be offered for accommodation in a 4-star hotel located near the Hellenic Pasteur Institute.",
      "search:taxonLabel": "Viruses",
      "search:publisherName": "European Virus Archive",
      "search:riskGroupLabel": "RG2",
      "search:collectionName": "HPI",
      "search:providerName": "HPI",
      "search:pathogenName": "Human respiratory syncytial virus, Influenza virus"
    },
    {
      "@type": "EVORAO:Service",
      "EVORAO:provider": {
        "@type": "EVORAO:Provider",
        "foaf:name": "HPI"
      },
      "EVORAO:refSku": "019S-06367",
      "@id": "urn:evorao:EVA:HPI:019S-06367",
      "EVORAO:accessPointUrl": "https://www.european-virus-archive.com/service/training-course-validation-verification-molecular-assays-viral-diagnostics",
      "dcterms:issued": "2026-04-03T13:54:15+02:00",
      "dcterms:modified": "2026-04-03T13:56:05+02:00",
      "dcterms:title": "Training Course: Validation &amp; Verification of Molecular Assays for Viral Diagnostics",
      "dcterms:description": "The Public Health Laboratories of Hellenic Pasteur Institute (HPI) invite laboratory professionals to participate in an intensive 3-day hands-on training course designed to enhance laboratory expertise in molecular diagnostics of viral infections. This comprehensive program covers the full workflow of assay validation and implementation, combining theory with practical insights.\r\nThe training will be tailored to the trainee’s needs and may include: \r\n1. Detection and typing of key viruses, \r\n2. Validation and Verification of molecular assays (quantification by standard curve analysis, evaluation of sensitivity and specificity, determination of Limit of Detection (LOD) and Limit of Quantification (LOQ), Levey-Jennings charts), \r\n3. Basic principles of biosafety and biosecurity, \r\n4. Basic principles of Quality Assurance of molecular assays. \r\nA special rate will be offered for accommodation in a 4-star hotel located near the Hellenic Pasteur Institute.",
      "EVORAO:unitDefinition": "3 days",
      "EVORAO:category": {
        "@type": "EVORAO:ProductCategory",
        "dcterms:title": "service"
      },
